  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'Architectural/Structural Design A.S. Degree - Cal-GETC GE' program map, Catalog 2026-27, published August 13, 2026 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/7738/PublishedPdf). GE Pattern: Cal-GETC. Official Total Units: 59-62; this seed models the first-listed/recommended path = 15 + 13 + 15 + 16 = 59 units (ENGL C1000 at 3 units per the official SCC English course page; Major Electives at 3 units each, the low end of the 3-4 range). Semester sums verified against the map's 15-16 / 13 / 15 / 16-18 headers. Distinct from the Architectural/Structural Design AS (Local GE) (map 7616). NOTE (documented map anomaly): the Sem 2 'GE Mathematical Concepts & Quantitative Reasoning' slot prints 0 units for Cal-GETC Area 2 — the 13-unit Sem 2 header only sums with 0 (3+4+3+0+3=13); modeled faithfully as a 0-unit generic Area 2 slot with a counselor-consultation note per the map's STEM-placement instruction. Consequently the low-path total is 59 units, below the 60-unit AA/AS minimum — this is the official map's arithmetic, transcribed without alteration. Choice slots: (1) GE ENGL C1000 / ** 488 / ESLW 340 H+ +, Area 1A — ENGL C1000 selected; (2) Elec INDIS 313 / *** HCD 310 — INDIS 313 selected; (3) ME Major Elective (minimum 6 units; choose 2): EDT 332, EDT 336, EDT 340, EDT 342, EDT 352, EDT 356, MATH 373, SURVY 300, SURVY 310 — EDT 332 and EDT 336 selected (first two listed), each modeled at 3 units. Documented prerequisites: EDT 312 requires EDT 310 (8-week terms: EDT 310 in 1st 8 weeks, EDT 312 in 2nd 8 weeks); EDT 316 requires EDT 310; EDT 320 requires EDT 310 or concurrent enrollment or equivalent; EDT 317 requires EDT 310; EDT 332 requires EDT 310 or concurrent enrollment; EDT 352 requires EDT 310 or concurrent enrollment; MATH 373 requires Intermediate Algebra or placement (STEM 3/5 placements not eligible); SURVY 310 requires EDT 310. Students not placing directly in ENGL C1000 take the ENGL 80/ENGL C1000 combo; ENGL 488 requires ESL 325; ESLW 340 requires ESL 325 or Los Rios assessment placement. Area 4 rule: the Sem 4 Area 4 course must be from a different discipline than the Sem 3 Area 4 course. GE Area 5C: the 1-unit Associate Lab Component is not required if a laboratory activity is included in the Area 5A or 5B course (per map note); modeled here as a generic 1-unit Area 5C slot. AA/AS requirements: 60 degree-applicable units with 2.0 GPA, 12 units within Los Rios, each required course 'C' or better, Cal-GETC Areas 1-6 with 'C' or better. Engineering Design Technology - Architectural/Structural Design, Science, Math, & Engineering Meta Majors. tccns mirrors SCC local course codes (California community colleges do not use TCCNS).",
